<title>FINLAND: FINNISH SAVINGS BANKS CUT REFERENCE RATE TO 4.00%.</title>
<headline>FINNISH SAVINGS BANKS CUT REFERENCE RATE TO 4.00%.</headline>
<dateline>HELSINKI 1996-10-14</dateline>
<text>
<p>Finland's independent savings banks said in a statement on Monday they would lower their joint lending reference rate to 4.00 percent from 4.50 percent on October 15.</p>
<p>The savings banks' reference rate is a weighted calculated average of the one-, three- and 12-month Helibor market interest rates and of the three-, five- and 10-year bond yields over 20 days, they said.</p>
<p>-- Helsinki newsroom +358-9-6805 0248</p>
